   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 192 of the laws of 2011, relating to authorizing\ncertain health care professionals licensed to practice in other jurisdictions\nto practice in this state in connection with an event sanctioned by New York\nRoad Runners, in relation to extending the provisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7625",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7625-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Chap 192 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Health",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7625\n\nSPONSOR: SERRANO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 192 of the laws of 2011,\nrelating to authorizing certain health care professionals licensed to\npractice in other jurisdictions to practice in this state in connection\nwith an event sanctioned by New York Road Runners, in relation to\nextending the provisions thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize certain licensed health care professionals from other\njurisdictions to practice in New York State with respect to six major\nevents sanctioned by New York Road Runners.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1-Authorizes that any person who is licensed to practice as a\nphysician, physician's assistant, massage therapist, physical therapist,\nchiropractor, dentist, optometrist, nurse, nurse practitioner, certified\nathletic trainer or podiatrist in another state or territory, who is in\ngood standing in such state or territory and who has been appointed by\nthe New York Road Runners to provide professional services at an event\nin this state sanctioned by the New York Road Runners, may provide such\nprofessional services to athletes and team personnel registered to train\nat a location in this state or registered to compete in an event\nconducted under the sanction of the New York Road Runners in the state\nwithout first being licensed pursuant to the provisions of Title 8 of\nthe Education Law. Such services may be provided only four days before\nthe following events, during the following events, and one day after the\nfollowing events:\n\nEvent                                Date\n\nStaten Island Half                   10.14.2018\nNew York City Marathon               11.04.2018\nBrooklyn Half                        05.19.2018\nBronx Half                           09.30.2018\nQueens 10K                           06.16.2018\nNew York City Half                   03.18.2018\n\nSection 2-Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThere  are  not  enough  health care professionals available, within the\nState of New York, to meet the needs of participants  in  certain  major\nevents  sanctioned  by the New York Road Runners, including the New York\nCity Marathon. Accordingly, it would be advantageous to  allow  licensed\nhealth  care  professionals, who are in good standing with their respec-\ntive state or territory, to provide such services here in New. York.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017- S4811;signed by the Governor\n\nThis is effectively a one year extender of legislation that has  histor-\nically passed each year, such as Chapter 39 of the Laws of 2016.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately and shall expire and be deemed repealed January 31, 2019.\n",
